-- title:
--   Cocompactness of the Fuchsian group of an order in a rational quaternion division algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated rational quaternion algebra. Assume: every nonzero $x\in B$ is a unit (so $B$ is a division algebra); $R\subseteq B$ is a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order in the sense of `IsOrder`, i.e. $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is all of $B$, and $R$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module; and $\iota\colon B\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ is an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism. Write $\Gamma=$ `fuchsianGroup R ι` for the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ obtained as the intersection of the image under $\iota$ (applied to units) of the subgroup of $B^\times$ generated by those units satisfying the predicate `IsUnitOf R`, with the kernel of the determinant homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})\to\mathbb{R}^\times$, so $\Gamma$ consists of determinant-one matrices. The conclusion is that there exists a compact subset $K$ of the upper half plane meeting every $\Gamma$-orbit: for every $\tau$ in the upper half plane there is $\gamma\in\Gamma$ with $\gamma\cdot\tau\in K$, the action being the Möbius action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$.
--
--   This is the classical cocompactness statement for the unit group of an order in an indefinite rational quaternion division algebra: the associated Shimura curve has no cusps. It feeds the analysis of the group $\Gamma$ used later, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_finset_forall_smul_eq_of_nrd_eq_of_not_isSquare`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_finset_forall_smul_eq_of_nrd_eq_of_not_isSquare) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.fuchsianGroup_discrete_neg_mem_and_exists_isCompact`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.fuchsianGroup_discrete_neg_mem_and_exists_isCompact).
